  <section id="about" class="section container">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I am a Ph.D. student in Computer Science and Engineering at The Chinese University of Hong Kong, advised by <a href="https://www.cse.cuhk.edu.hk/~byu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prof. Bei Yu</a>. My research has two closely connected directions: <strong>LLM4EDA / AI4EDA</strong> and <strong>3D IC design automation</strong>.</p>
      <p>On the AI side, I study multi-modal circuit representations, cross-stage knowledge distillation, and LLM-based verification and optimization. On the 3D IC side, I develop legality-aware RTL-to-GDS flows and early-stage timing models for hybrid-bonded designs. My current interests include tool-using agents for chip implementation and the interaction of data paths, bonding parasitics, and clock networks in setup/hold timing closure.</p>
      <p>Before joining CUHK, I received my master's degree in Electronic Information from the University of Chinese Academy of Sciences and the Institute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences, advised by Prof. Xiaowei Li and Prof. Huawei Li at the State Key Laboratory of Processors. I received my bachelor's degree in Microelectronics Science and Technology from Peking University, and have industrial EDA experience with CASTEST on fault simulation and ISO 26262-oriented functional safety analysis.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="news" class="section container">
    <h2>News</h2>
    <div class="news-box">
      <p><strong>2026/11</strong> · ASP-DAC 2027: CU-3D is an invited paper; HOIST and Logic Resynthesis for Cross-Die Dependencies are accepted. I am a co-corresponding author of HOIST.</p>
      <p><strong>2026/11</strong> · MigSizer is accepted at ICCD 2026 for physical-aware analog/RF circuit migration.</p>
      <p><strong>2026/07</strong> · ICCAD 2026: Distill3D, LibPilot, and ChatFCM accepted.</p>
      <p><strong>2026/05</strong> · IEEE TCAD Early Access: "Bit-Compressed Concurrent Fault Simulation with Efficient Fault List" is online.</p>
      <p><strong>2026/05</strong> · ICML 2026: AnalogVerifier accepted.</p>
      <p><strong>2026/04</strong> · ICLR 2026: CircuitNet 3.0 accepted as a poster paper.</p>
      <p><strong>2026/04</strong> · DAC 2026: ATLAS accepted for FIT prediction with asynchronous topological learning.</p>
      <p><strong>2025/12</strong> · 2nd Place at EDAthon 2025, Programming Competition on Electronic Design Automation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="research" class="section container">
    <h2>Research Interests</h2>
    <div class="focus-grid">
      <article class="focus-card">
        <h3>LLM4EDA / AI4EDA</h3>
        <p>Circuit representation learning, knowledge distillation, and LLM-based design. My current interests include domain-adaptive continued pretraining, SFT, and tool-feedback reinforcement learning, grounded in functional and physical verification.</p>
        <p class="focus-links"><a href="#pub-circuitnet">CircuitNet 3.0</a> · <a href="#pub-rtldistil">RTLDistil</a> · <a href="#pub-chatfcm">ChatFCM</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="focus-card">
        <h3>3D IC Design Automation</h3>
        <p>Legality-aware RTL-to-GDS flows, hybrid-bonding integration, and cross-stage timing prediction. I connect physical implementation with post-route analysis and setup/hold timing closure.</p>
        <p class="focus-links"><a href="#pub-cu3d">CU-3D</a> · <a href="#pub-distill3d">Distill3D</a> · <a href="#pub-resynthesis">3D Logic Resynthesis</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="focus-card focus-support">
        <h3>Fault Simulation and Functional Safety</h3>
        <p>A complementary foundation in hardware-aware simulation, parallel algorithms, and ISO 26262-oriented analysis, developed through <a href="#pub-domsim">DomSim</a>, EPICS, ETPG, and industrial EDA work.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

