  <section id="experience" class="section container">
    <h2>Research Experience</h2>
    <div class="experience-list">
      <article>
        <div class="time">May 2024 — Present</div>
        <h3>LLM4EDA / AI4EDA and 3D IC Design Automation</h3>
        <ul><li><strong>Circuit learning:</strong> developed multi-modal representations and cross-stage timing/power models through MOSS, RTLDistil, CircuitNet 3.0, and Distill3D.</li><li><strong>LLM-based EDA:</strong> designed and implemented functional coverage generation methods and tool-based validation in an industry-academic project; contributed to ChatFCM and knowledge-constrained library tuning with LibPilot.</li><li><strong>3D implementation:</strong> developed a research RTL-to-GDS flow integrating hybrid-bonding structures, clock-tree synthesis, routing, parasitic extraction, and timing analysis.</li><li><strong>Current focus:</strong> tool-using agents that improve chip designs under functional and physical constraints, evaluated through post-route results and tool-use costs.</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="time">Jul. 2023 — Mar. 2025</div>
        <h3>Fault Simulation Research · State Key Laboratory of Processors, ICT, CAS</h3>
        <ul><li>Developed hardware-aware parallel simulation using dominator-tree partitioning, strongly connected components, and pattern parallelism.</li><li>DomSim achieved a 10.29× average speedup over the commercial baseline in its published experiments; EPICS achieved 5.94× while preserving fault coverage in its experiments.</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="time">Sep. 2021 — Jan. 2025</div>
        <h3>Industrial Experience · CASTEST</h3>
        <ul><li>Developed core fault simulation algorithms and contributed to tool integration, multi-core optimization, and industrial requirements validation.</li><li>Integrated parallel simulation into ISO 26262-oriented functional safety analysis workflows for automotive chips.</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="time">Sep. 2020 — Jun. 2022</div>
        <h3>RRAM-Based True Random Number Generator · PKU Undergraduate Thesis</h3>
        <ul><li>Designed and implemented an RRAM-based random number generator.</li><li>Evaluated randomness using the NIST statistical test suite.</li></ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

